entries[391429] = { ["name"] = "Fodder to the Flame", ["text"] = "Spectral Sight has 30 sec increased cooldown and now reveals a condemned demon for 25 sec. [ Vengeance : Fel Devastation /\n\nHavoc\nEye Beam ] and Throw Glaive deal lethal damage to the demon, granting 20% increased damage for 15 sec.\n\nThe demon explodes on death, dealing (192.5% of Attack Power) Shadow damage to nearby enemies and healing you for 20% of your maximum health. The explosion deals reduced damage beyond 5 targets." }
entries[391430] = { ["name"] = "Fodder to the Flame", ["text"] = "Instant 2 min cooldown\nYour damaging abilities have a chance to call forth a demon from the Theater of Pain for 25 sec. Throw Glaive deals lethal damage to the demon, which explodes on death, dealing (192.5% of Attack Power) Shadow damage to nearby enemies and healing you for 20% of your maximum health. The explosion deals reduced damage beyond 5 targets." }
entries[391431] = { ["name"] = "Windswept Hochenblume", ["text"] = "5 yd range\n2.5 sec cast\nHochenblume is the most common herb found across the Dragon Isles. It can be found in practically any terrain, growing wherever possible.\n\nHerbs that grow up high or in particularly windy regions like the Ohn'ahran Plains can absorb the elemental power of air. Powerful gusts of wind is unleashed when these herbs are gathered, knocking the herbalist away. However, it is an effective way to find Rousing Air.\n\nHerbalists specialized in Windswept herbs will gain the following effect when gathering:\n\nWindswept :\nWhen falling farther than 40 yd, a powerful gust of wind slows your descent." }
entries[391441] = { ["name"] = "Saxifrage", ["text"] = "5 yd range\n2.5 sec cast\nSaxifrage is a sturdy herb that can grow in a multitude of places. While generally found in rugged locations like mountains or on cliffs, it can also be found upon the open plains or scarcely within volcanic regions." }
entries[391444] = { ["name"] = "Bubble Poppy", ["text"] = "5 yd range\n2.5 sec cast\nBubble Poppy is a delicate herb that grows in the aquatic locales of the Dragon Isles. It grows along the rivers, coasts, and inside damp caves.\n\nDespite its unique appearance, the Bubble Poppy flower isn't particularly useful. Rather, the watery, fungal orb that forms at its base is where the real value lies." }
