entries[391492] = { ["name"] = "Decayed Hochenblume", ["text"] = "5 yd range\n2.5 sec cast\nHochenblume is the most common herb found across the Dragon Isles. It can be found in practically any terrain, growing wherever possible.\n\nHerbs exposed to the essence of Decay become wilted versions of their former selves. The plants are still usable, but any would-be gatherers are exposed to the Decay, afflicting them with illness. It can be worth it though, as these herbs are a dependable source of Rousing Decay.\n\nHerbalists specialized in Decayed herbs will gain the following effect when gathering:\n\nControlled Decay :\nBecome empowered by present Decay magic. Your Overload Elemental Herb spell is recharging at 400% the normal rate." }
entries[391493] = { ["name"] = "Smoldering Ore", ["text"] = "Instant\nSet ablaze by a molten ore vein. Frequently suffering fire damage over 20 sec or until submerged in water." }
entries[391496] = { ["name"] = "Titan-Touched Hochenblume", ["text"] = "5 yd range\n2.5 sec cast\nHochenblume is the most common herb found across the Dragon Isles. It can be found in practically any terrain, growing wherever possible.\n\nHerbs that grow in areas rich in the influence of the Titans, such as the Waking Shores or Thaldraszus, may similarly become empowered. These types of herbs grant a boon to the herbalist who stumbles upon them, as well as some Rousing Order.\n\nHerbalists specialized in Titan-Touched herbs will gain the following effect when gathering:\n\nEnlightened Potential :\nSpeed increased by 15%. Gatherers specialized in Titan-Touched nodes will also have their secondary stats increased by 3%." }
entries[391497] = { ["name"] = "Whelp Blast" }
entries[391498] = { ["name"] = "Infurious Hochenblume", ["text"] = "5 yd range\n2.5 sec cast\nHochenblume is the most common herb found across the Dragon Isles. It can be found in practically any terrain, growing wherever possible.\n\nFound growing only in places of embroiled conflict, rumor has it that these herbs have gained magical properties from the ire of those fighting around them.\n\nGain the following effect when gathering:\n\nFury of Battle :\nYou have a chance when slaying enemy players to gain Rousing Ire. Lasts 2 min.\n\nFurther mining or herb gathering extends the duration." }
entries[391499] = { ["name"] = "Infurious Saxifrage", ["text"] = "5 yd range\n2.5 sec cast\nSaxifrage is a sturdy herb that can grow in a multitude of places. While generally found in rugged locations like mountains or on cliffs, it can also be found upon the open plains or scarcely within volcanic regions.\n\nFound growing only in places of embroiled conflict, rumor has it that these herbs have gained magical properties from the ire of those fighting around them.\n\nGain the following effect when gathering:\n\nFury of Battle :\nYou have a chance when slaying enemy players to gain Rousing Ire. Lasts 2 min.\n\nFurther mining or herb gathering extends the duration." }
entries[391500] = { ["name"] = "Decayed Saxifrage", ["text"] = "5 yd range\n2.5 sec cast\nSaxifrage is a sturdy herb that can grow in a multitude of places. While generally found in rugged locations like mountains or on cliffs, it can also be found upon the open plains or scarcely within volcanic regions.\n\nHerbs exposed to the essence of Decay become wilted versions of their former selves. The plants are still usable, but any would-be gatherers are exposed to the Decay, afflicting them with illness. It can be worth it though, as these herbs are a dependable source of Rousing Decay.\n\nHerbalists specialized in Decayed herbs will gain the following effect when gathering:\n\nControlled Decay :\nBecome empowered by present Decay magic. Your Overload Elemental Herb spell is recharging at 400% the normal rate." }
entries[391501] = { ["name"] = "Frigid Saxifrage", ["text"] = "5 yd range\n2.5 sec cast\nSaxifrage is a sturdy herb that can grow in a multitude of places. While generally found in rugged locations like mountains or on cliffs, it can also be found upon the open plains or scarcely within volcanic regions.\n\nWhen exposed to colder climates or are located near sources of water, they can become infused with elemental frost. Gathering these types of herbs will cover the ground in slick ice, but the herbalist will be rewarded with Rousing Frost for their efforts.\n\nHerbalists specialized in Frigid herbs will gain the following effect when gathering:\n\nFrigid Petals :\nEnvelops you in a cloud of frost which causes any enemy who approaches too close to you to become frozen momentarily." }
entries[391502] = { ["name"] = "Lush Saxifrage", ["text"] = "5 yd range\n2.5 sec cast\nSaxifrage is a sturdy herb that can grow in a multitude of places. While generally found in rugged locations like mountains or on cliffs, it can also be found upon the open plains or scarcely within volcanic regions.\n\nSome herbs grow particularly well and thrive for any number of reasons, regardless of climate or location. Herbalists who come across these rare nodes can retrieve additional usable materials." }
entries[391503] = { ["name"] = "Titan-Touched Saxifrage", ["text"] = "5 yd range\n2.5 sec cast\nSaxifrage is a sturdy herb that can grow in a multitude of places. While generally found in rugged locations like mountains or on cliffs, it can also be found upon the open plains or scarcely within volcanic regions.\n\nHerbs that grow in areas rich in the influence of the Titans, such as the Waking Shores or Thaldraszus, may similarly become empowered. These types of herbs grant a boon to the herbalist who stumbles upon them, as well as some Rousing Order.\n\nHerbalists specialized in Titan-Touched herbs will gain the following effect when gathering:\n\nEnlightened Potential :\nSpeed increased by 15%. Gatherers specialized in Titan-Touched nodes will also have their secondary stats increased by 3%." }
entries[391504] = { ["name"] = "Windswept Saxifrage", ["text"] = "5 yd range\n2.5 sec cast\nSaxifrage is a sturdy herb that can grow in a multitude of places. While generally found in rugged locations like mountains or on cliffs, it can also be found upon the open plains or scarcely within volcanic regions.\n\nHerbs that grow up high or in particularly windy regions like the Ohn'ahran Plains can absorb the elemental power of air. Powerful gusts of wind is unleashed when these herbs are gathered, knocking the herbalist away. However, it is an effective way to find Rousing Air.\n\nHerbalists specialized in Windswept herbs will gain the following effect when gathering:\n\nWindswept :\nWhen falling farther than 40 yd, a powerful gust of wind slows your descent." }
entries[391505] = { ["name"] = "Infurious Bubble Poppy", ["text"] = "5 yd range\n2.5 sec cast\nBubble Poppy is a delicate herb that grows in the aquatic locales of the Dragon Isles. It grows along the rivers, coasts, and inside damp caves.\n\nDespite its unique appearance, the Bubble Poppy flower isn't particularly useful. Rather, the watery, fungal orb that forms at its base is where the real value lies.\n\nFound growing only in places of embroiled conflict, rumor has it that these herbs have gained magical properties from the ire of those fighting around them.\n\nGain the following effect when gathering:\n\nFury of Battle :\nYou have a chance when slaying enemy players to gain Rousing Ire. Lasts 2 min.\n\nFurther mining or herb gathering extends the duration." }
entries[391506] = { ["name"] = "Infurious Writhebark", ["text"] = "5 yd range\n2.5 sec cast\nWrithebark is a verdant herb found on the Dragon Isles. It can be found where there is an abundance of trees or foliage.\n\nFound growing only in places of embroiled conflict, rumor has it that these herbs have gained magical properties from the ire of those fighting around them.\n\nGain the following effect when gathering:\n\nFury of Battle :\nYou have a chance when slaying enemy players to gain Rousing Ire. Lasts 2 min.\n\nFurther mining or herb gathering extends the duration." }
